# HMRC contacts finder

Route a person to a support channel that exists, starting from the subject and showing the channel and its stated scope. The tax-authority contacts in the source have no household equivalent, so this page covers integration documentation and verified maintenance contacts only. An urgent fault must never end at an ordinary feedback form. Scope, result count, empty states, focus and the no-JavaScript fallback follow the [shared finder behaviour](../finder.html#finder-shared-contract).

## When to use it

Use it to route a person to an integration’s documentation or a verified maintenance contact. Start with the subject, then show the channel and its stated scope.

## Home Assistant boundary

Do not invent phone numbers, availability or response times. Private contact details need the household’s own access controls. Send an urgent problem somewhere that treats it as urgent.

